<description>&lt;p&gt;Elders are being urged to use their influence to prevent conflict and protect communities while a Sudanese official accuses Ethiopia and South Sudan of fuelling regional instability. Armed violence continues with a boda-boda rider shot dead by an armed passenger in Wau, a Christian woman killed for refusing a forced marriage, two Kapoeta youth killed after an SSPDF arrest, and the Kapoeta South Commissioner confirming the killing of an SPLM secretary and a friend. Clashes between SSPDF and SPLA-IO have forced over 300 IDPs to flee shelters in Tambura County, and the Ministry of Gender is reviewing draft safe-house guidelines for GBV survivors. Two battle-related deaths were recorded in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Social News XYZ&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiUEFVX3lxTE1pbkFIUFo0MnJCaWJMejVKbGRkZkRNZ3BVQ296Z21IU0RQZV9HVkFCbk1FRl9lekdwelRjR25ISVdCNVZnM0RwLTZTam5aUmU4?oc=5&quot;&gt;Sudan Tribune&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;OkayAfrica&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;Eye Radio&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxPeExHSlFyZkVkaVItZVRMaW1nM2hHSkdvMUNjdV9yRUo0UHBFY01qNTRweGRuRVlEVjJ1bXd3ZWQ2ek05MmZhUjFaaFBoejVTc09XWWstSC1DQl9vRzdJRThFWjh4cTBhaXdMZkxtcl9LR0tqaTBIcDRmSW9JYmUxSXpsNENWbkFDM1IwbjBiWDBNYU9qMUMxNzJrSXpibU1SdjdSbUFVbmZoWEdKenQ1WWRR?oc=5&quot;&gt;Premier Christian News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMikwFBVV95cUxPbWxPcGZSSS1OMkhoYUt4V2dWaG5semQ2ZllsSjZZTTBNOEYzU3dxaFluNmp3VHQxNUtIZXdHSml2RFQwRm94SzJmZ3ZFWEs4aVZXSDNEeXNsMEFHMHdJMGlvSDhValpMa0xTZkJVTDZ5WmMtbjE1Q0x3WEVXaFZYbXBJVVEzYXV0ZVNnaEdxSmdwZVk?oc=5&qu